.TH RUSTYPE-LINUX 1 "November 2026" "Rustype 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustype-linux \- Vietnamese input method bus and engine for GNOME Shell on Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustype-linux
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B rustype-linux
.BR \-\-activate " [" \-\-restart ]
.br
.B rustype-linux
.B \-\-deactivate
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rustype-linux
is the Rustype input method for Linux. It is a single process, written in Rust with only the standard library, that speaks the IBus protocol to GNOME Shell and its libibus clients and runs the Rustype engine in the same process. It replaces both
.B ibus-daemon
and the former IBus engine.
.PP
Only GNOME Shell on Wayland is supported. Flatpak applications, KDE, Sway, Hyprland, other IBus engines and the IBus emoji panel are not supported. The
.B ibus
package stays installed because GNOME Shell needs libibus, but
.B ibus-daemon
does not run while Rustype is in use.
.PP
Normally the process is started by systemd as the user unit
.IR org.freedesktop.IBus.session.GNOME.service ,
which the installer points at
.BR "rustype-linux --own-session-name" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Run system diagnostic checks: installation, the bus, component registration, GNOME input sources, the GNOME Shell focus extension, and the configuration file. Prints a recommendation for each failing check. It exits with status 1 when any check fails; warnings alone keep status 0.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-config
Create the default configuration file at \fI~/.config/rustype/config\fR if it does not exist.
.TP
.B \-\-activate
Make Rustype usable in the current user's GNOME session. Does nothing when the session has no
.IR org.freedesktop.IBus.session.GNOME.service
unit, so it is safe to run for any user. Otherwise it creates the configuration file if it is missing and, on the first run only, adds Rustype to the GNOME input sources (after the first entry, or as the only entry when the list is empty) and enables the focus extension. A stamp file \fI~/.config/rustype/activated\fR records that this was done, so a source the user later removes is not added back. The command never prompts and always exits with status 0.
.TP
.B \-\-restart
With \fB\-\-activate\fR, reload the systemd user manager and restart the IBus unit without waiting, but only when its main process runs a different executable, for example ibus-daemon, or an older rustype-linux that was replaced by an upgrade.
.TP
.B \-\-deactivate
Remove Rustype from the GNOME input sources and delete the stamp file, so that the next \fB\-\-activate\fR adds it again. The configuration file is kept.
.TP
.B \-\-feed
Read keystrokes from standard input and print the resulting text, without running a bus. Useful for quick checks of the Telex and VNI engine, for example:
.B echo "Vieetj Nam" | rustype-linux --feed
.TP
.B \-\-own\-session\-name
Connect to the session bus (\fBDBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS\fR) and claim the well-known name
.BR org.freedesktop.IBus .
This is the option the systemd unit uses.
.TP
.BI \-\-address " unix:path=PATH"
Serve the bus on the given Unix socket. Without this option the socket is \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rustype/bus\fR. Only \fBunix:path=\fR addresses are supported.
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Take over an address file that points at a live bus. The previous process is not stopped by this option.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print the software version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display command-line help information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUSTYPE_DEBUG
When set (e.g. \fBRUSTYPE_DEBUG=1\fR), writes diagnostic logging to standard error. Debug output only records hardware key codes and input states, never the text typed or committed.
.TP
.B IBUS_ADDRESS, IBUS_ADDRESS_FILE
Used by clients to find the bus. \fBIBUS_ADDRESS_FILE\fR names the address file that the process writes.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME
Locations of the default socket, the configuration, and the address file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustype/config
Main configuration file. Controls the input method (Telex or VNI), display mode, orthography, English word restoration, macros, and per-application modes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustype/macro
Macro file with abbreviation mappings, one pair per line: \fIabbreviation:expansion\fR. Compatible with Unikey macro files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustype/words
Custom list of English words that should never receive Vietnamese tone marks.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustype/activated
Stamp written by \fB\-\-activate\fR. While it exists, activation does not add the input source again.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/dev.namtr.RustypeActivate.desktop
Installed by the package. It runs \fB\-\-activate\fR at each GNOME login, so the user and later logins are covered.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ibus/bus/
Address file for the bus, written by the process so that libibus clients can find it.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/org.freedesktop.IBus.session.GNOME.service.d/rustype.conf
Vendor drop-in installed by the package. It points the systemd user unit at
.BR rustype-linux .
A source install writes an equivalent drop-in under \fI~/.config/systemd/user/\fR.
.SH PRIVACY & SECURITY
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNo network code:\fR the process uses only the standard library and a local Unix socket. It does not open network connections.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNo keystroke logs:\fR keystrokes are held in memory while a word is being formed and discarded when it is committed or the focus changes. Nothing typed is written to disk.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPassword and PIN fields:\fR keystrokes pass straight to the application when the input field reports the password or PIN purpose.
